.TH CCHAN_TRY_RECV 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cchan_try_recv \- try to receive a message with no block
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cthreadcomm.h>

ccol_retval_t cchan_try_recv(cchan *ch, cmessage_t *target_buf);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Takes a message from the queue that the channel picks for the calling
thread, if one is there, and returns at once when that queue is empty.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
ch          Channel to receive from
target_buf  Buffer that gets the message
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success         - A message was received. The caller must free
                       target_buf->data.
ccol_invalid_args    - ch or target_buf is NULL
ccol_container_empty - The chosen queue is empty
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
This call never blocks. The direction comes from the ID of the
calling thread, as described in cchan_recv(3).
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cchan_recv (3),
.BR cchan_timed_recv (3)
